{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"da0caa962c4983e965a84c99efeee0c7e7a8ece98a4479190ddef4e23a94502b","digest":{"component_or_area":"CLI parser / help formatting","key_entities":["RebarHelpFormatter","argparse.HelpFormatter","src/rebar/_cli/_parser.py","metrics.build","audit.build","bridge_arms.build_fsck","bridge_arms.build_probe","src/rebar/_cli/help/bridge-fsck.txt","docs/cli-reference.md","gen_cli_help.py","gen_cli_reference.py","tests/interfaces/contracts/test_parser_formatter_pinned.py"],"problem_keywords":["argparse","help-generation","py3.13","regression","cli-formatter","width-inconsistency"],"propositions":["Four advanced parser factories (metrics, audit, bridge-fsck, bridge-probe) use stdlib argparse.HelpFormatter instead of the version-pinned RebarHelpFormatter, creating width inconsistency (78 vs 80) and py3.13 staleness risk in committed help artifacts","py3.13 argparse divergences in option rendering and usage wrapping could cause help artifacts to silently diverge on py3.13 CI only, making gen_cli_help.py --check stale without detection","No contract test enforces that all help-backed (rendered) routes use RebarHelpFormatter, allowing regression if new formatters are introduced","Switching the four factories to RebarHelpFormatter and regenerating artifacts consolidates help width to canonical 80 and closes the py3.13 divergence gap for rendered advanced routes"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787394094088147001,"uuid":"a97835ba-9988-4333-9ea4-0f3d30de10e0"}